The first part of your question would work fine locally, no problem; but for it to work from our server (glimmer.rstudio.com <http://glimmer.rstudio.com>), your SQL Server would need to be publicly accessible over the internet (which is generally just not a great practice security-wise). Or else, you would have to set up a scheduled task on one of your machines to dump your SQL Server data to a .csv file periodically and upload it to our servers. Then your Shiny app can do read.csv and use the head function to show just the top input$n rows.

But regarding password protection, it is explicitly not supported on our servers right now nor by Shiny Server. There are a couple of options you have if running Linux (including cloud based like Amazon EC2), but if you only have access to Windows servers then we do not currently have an answer for you (but are hoping to later in the year).

