By the way, even if just running locally it is very very important that when you form the SQL query string you do it like this:

vws <- sqlQuery(dbConnect, paste("SELECT TOP", as.numeric(input$n), "Datum, Sava, P1, P2, P3 FROM VWS  ORDER BY ID DESC"))

Without the "as.numeric" it would be easy for a malicious user to set input$n to "10 1; DROP TABLE VWS; --" for example, which would cause your whole database table to be erased! (This is called SQL injection <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SQL_injection> and is probably the most common way websites get hacked.)

